  "text": "Recipe: Uthapam & Almond Chutney\nCreator: Meera Arun\nCategory: Uthapam\nIngredients: Whole Oat Groats: 1 cup, Brown Sona Masoori Rice: 1 cup, Urad Dal: 1/2 cup, Toor Dal: 1/2 cup, Curry Leaves: 3-4 sprigs, Shallots: 5-6, Garlic: 3-4 cloves, Dried Red Chili: 4, Black Pepper: 1/2 tsp, Cumin Seeds: 1/2 tsp, Salt: (to taste), Arugula or any Greens: two 5 oz bags, Almonds: some soaked, Ginger: a small piece, Green Chilly: a small, Daliya (roasted split chana dal): a few Tbsp, Water: some\nCooking methods: soak, grind, blend, cook\nInstructions: Soak oat groats, rice, urad dal & toor dal overnight.\nNext morning, grind them along with other ingredients (except salt and chopped greens). Keep it aside for 30 mins.\nAdd chopped greens and salt (if using) just before making oil-free uttapam (thicker dosas) on a griddle.\nALMOND CHUTNEY: Blend some soaked almonds, a small piece of ginger, a small shallot, green chilly, a few Tbsp of daliya (roasted split chana dal), some curry leaves and a little salt (if using), along with some water.\nNotes: Almond Chutney (sub-recipe)",
